#!/bin/bash
# Interactive shell for the showroom OpenShift Cluster Terminal. oc is baked into
# the image; the merged kubeconfig for every deployed cluster is injected onto the
# shared disk at /showroom/kube/config (root-owned 0644 — readable, not writable).
#
# Two runtime contexts:
#  * troshkad (podman): wetty runs this as root, so we prep uid-1000's home and
#    drop to the unprivileged lab user via setpriv (util-linux/glibc; no sudo/PAM).
#  * KubeVirt native (restricted SCC): the container already runs as a random
#    non-root uid with no CAP_SETUID, so setpriv would fail ("setresuid failed:
#    Operation not permitted", exit 127). Detect that and exec the shell as the
#    current uid using a writable HOME instead.
export PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

if [ "$(id -u)" = "0" ]; then
    # Running as root (podman): prep the lab user's home + kubeconfig, then drop.
    export HOME=/home/labuser
    export KUBECONFIG="$HOME/.kube/config"
    if [ -f /showroom/kube/config ]; then
        install -d -o 1000 -g 1000 -m 0700 "$HOME/.kube"
        install -o 1000 -g 1000 -m 0600 /showroom/kube/config "$KUBECONFIG"
    fi
    cd "$HOME" 2>/dev/null || cd /tmp
    exec setpriv --reuid=1000 --regid=1000 --init-groups /bin/bash
fi

# Running as a non-root (restricted-SCC) uid: no privilege drop possible or needed.
# Use a writable HOME (the labuser home is not owned by this uid) for the kubeconfig.
if [ -z "$HOME" ] || [ ! -w "$HOME" ]; then
    export HOME=/tmp
fi
export KUBECONFIG="$HOME/.kube/config"
if [ -f /showroom/kube/config ]; then
    mkdir -p "$HOME/.kube"
    cp /showroom/kube/config "$KUBECONFIG" 2>/dev/null && chmod 0600 "$KUBECONFIG" 2>/dev/null
fi
cd "$HOME" 2>/dev/null || cd /tmp
exec /bin/bash
